    "text": "# Investigation note: metric M369375, reporting month 2026-10-31\n\n**1. Executive finding**\nM369375 sits in the provisional **Green** band for 2026-10-31. Its provisional rate is **35.3% (6 of 17)**, below the provisional 45% Green threshold. Under the band rule you supplied (a higher rate is worse), it is not a concern this month. There is one data point to check before relying on that reading (see section 7).\n\n**2. Current status and period (2026-10-31)**\n- There are 24 metric rows, one each for 24 applications.\n- Compliance status: 6 Compliant, 11 Non_Compliant, 2 Pending, 5 Not_Applicable.\n- The denominator of 17 is the 6 Compliant plus the 11 Non_Compliant rows. Pending and Not_Applicable rows are left out, which matches the inferred EXCLUDES_PENDING scope.\n- The numerator of 6 is exactly the 6 Compliant rows.\n\n**3. Movement against the prior month (provisional)**\n- The rate fell from 52.6% (10 of 19) on 2026-09-30 to 35.3% (6 of 17), a change of **−17.3 percentage points**.\n- The rate is now the lowest of the 12 months. It ranged from 37.5% to 63.6% in earlier months.\n- The population also changed: rows went from 27 to 24 and the denominator from 19 to 17. So part of the movement may come from which applications reported, not only from changes in status. I have not run the check that separates continuing applications from new or departing ones.\n**4. Main contributors (2026-10-31, observed)**\n- **Non-compliant rows by super division:** Super_Division_02, 03, 04, 05 and 08 have 2 each, Super_Division_07 has 1 and Super_Division_06 has 0. No single organisation stands out.\n- **Legal entities:** Legal_Entity_20 is the only one with more than one non-compliant row. It has 2, from applications EON792119 and EON960700, which belong to different super divisions. Every other legal entity has at most 1.\n- **Reasons for non-compliance (11 rows):** Test_Failed 7, Open_Findings_Outstanding 2, Remediation_Overdue 2.\n**5. Testing and exception observations (observed)**\n- 17 rows have a completed test with a result: 10 Fail and 7 Pass. Failed tests rose from 7 the month before.\n- 1 row is Test_Pending, 5 are No_Test (all Not_Applicable with reason No_Test_Required) and 1 is Exempt.\n- The Exempt row (EON964491) is counted as Compliant with reason Exemption_Conditions_Met, so it is part of the numerator.\n- Mismatches between test result and status:\n  - EON952255 passed its test but is Non_Compliant (Open_Findings_Outstanding).\n  - EON682214 passed its test but is Pending (Result_Under_Review).\n\n**6. Areas for further investigation (hypotheses, not findings)**\n- Whether the 17-point fall comes from status changes in the same applications or from a different set of applications reporting. The month-on-month movement check for each application and the composition check have not been run.\n- The two Legal_Entity_20 rows: is this a coincidence, or something they share?\n- Why some passed tests sit with Non_Compliant or Pending status.\n- How the Exempt row is treated in the numerator.\n\n**7. Limitations**\n- **Direction of the rate.** In this data the numerator rows are exactly the Compliant rows. If \"higher is worse\" is right, a falling rate means fewer Compliant rows. The non-compliant count went up from 9 to 11 and failed tests from 7 to 10 over the same month. The meaning of the numerator has not been confirmed by the client, so please check the band direction before relying on \"Green\".\n- The rate, the bands and the movement figures are all provisional. They are not client targets and should not be compared across metrics.\n- The sample is small (17 denominator rows), so a change of one or two rows moves the rate by several points.\n- No metric name, family or business definition is available. No causes, owners or completed remediation are recorded or implied.\n- All names are synthetic.",
